<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Peloponnese</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Morea</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Morea was the name used from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> to the 19th century for the Peloponnese, the large peninsula of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>. It was divided after 1204 between the Frankish Principality of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaea">Achaea</a>, Venetian ports and the Byzantine <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/despotate-of-the-morea">Despotate of the Morea</a>, and conquered by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> by 1460. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> held it again as the Kingdom of the Morea from 1685 to 1715.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/peloponnese.jpg" alt="Peloponnese" width="320" height="277" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SilentResident,Philly boy92 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Location_map_of_Peloponnese_(Greece).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
